<p>A GST invoice in PDF format ensures professional presentation and legal compliance for businesses across India.</p>


<h2>What is a GST Invoice?</h2>
<p>Under GST law in India, every registered business must issue a tax invoice containing mandatory details such as GSTIN, invoice number, tax breakup and HSN/SAC codes.</p>


<div class="row">

    <div class="col">
        <h2>Mandatory Fields in GST Invoice Excel Format</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Invoice Number (Unique & Serial)</li>
            <li>Invoice Date</li>
            <li>Supplier Name, Address & GSTIN</li>
            <li>Buyer Name, Address & GSTIN (if registered)</li>
            <li>HSN (Goods) / SAC (Services)</li>
            <li>Taxable Value</li>
            <li>CGST + SGST (Intra-state) OR IGST (Inter-state)</li>
            <li>Total Invoice Amount</li>
        </ul>

        <hr />

        <h2>Related Pages</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="/gst-invoice-format/excel">GST Invoice Format in Excel</a></li>
            <li><a href="/gst-invoice-for-small-business">GST Invoice for Small Business</a></li>
        </ul>

    </div>

    <div class="col">
        <h2>Sample GST Calculation in Excel</h2>
        <p>
            Example: Product Value ₹10,000<br>
            GST @@18% → CGST 9% = ₹900 + SGST 9% = ₹900<br>
            Total = ₹11,800
        </p>

        <hr />

        <h2>What Should GST Invoice PDF Include?</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Supplier GSTIN</li>
            <li>Invoice number & date</li>
            <li>Buyer details</li>
            <li>HSN/SAC code</li>
            <li>Taxable value</li>
            <li>CGST/SGST or IGST breakup</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            👉 <a asp-controller="Invoice" asp-action="Index">Generate GST Invoice PDF Online</a>
        </p>

    </div>
</div>



